@startuml seq-receive-only
title Receive-only peer applies an inbound event and acks back

actor "Source A" as A
queue "RabbitMQ" as Q
participant "propagator (this lib)" as Lib
participant "hmacAuth.clients" as Core
database "Redis (cursor)" as R

A -> Q : publish hmac-<peer>.queue\n(eventId, propagationSecret=peer)

Q -> Lib : consume
Lib -> Lib : decode + timingSafeEqual propagationSecret
Lib -> R : read cursor
R --> Lib : null or (lastTs, lastEventId)
Lib -> Lib : isStrictlyNewer? yes
Lib -> Core : setSecretHash or delete
Lib -> R : write cursor (ts, eventId)
Lib -> Q : publish ACK back\nhmac-<source>.queue\npropagationSecret = ""
Lib -> Q : ack original message

note over Lib
  Receive-only: no management -> no
  fetchSourcePropagationSecret. ACK is
  published with empty secret; the
  source warn-drops it but the local
  apply already happened.
end note

@enduml
